.IX Title "Koha::Devel::CI::IncrementalRuns 3pm"
.TH Koha::Devel::CI::IncrementalRuns 3pm "2026-06-25" "perl v5.32.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
Koha::Devel::CI::IncrementalRuns \- A module for managing incremental CI runs in Koha development.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    use Koha::Devel::CI::IncrementalRuns;
\&
\&    my $ci = Koha::Devel::CI::IncrementalRuns\->new({
\&        context      => \*(Aqtidy\*(Aq,
\&    });
\&
\&    my @files_to_test = $ci\->get_files_to_test(\*(Aqpl\*(Aq);
\&    $ci\->report_results($results);
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Koha::Devel::CI::IncrementalRuns is a module designed to manage incremental \s-1CI\s0 runs in the Koha development environment. It provides functionality to determine which files need to be tested based on previous \s-1CI\s0 runs and to report the results of those tests.
.SH "METHODS"
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS "new"
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 9
\&    my $ci = Koha::Devel::CI::IncrementalRuns\->new({
\&        incremental_run => 1,
\&        git_repo_dir    => \*(Aq/path/to/repo\*(Aq,
\&        repo_url        => \*(Aqhttps://gitlab.com/koha\-community/koha\-ci\-results.git\*(Aq,
\&        report          => 1,
\&        token           => \*(Aqyour_token\*(Aq,
\&        test_name       => \*(Aqtest_name\*(Aq,
\&        context         => \*(Aqtidy\*(Aq,
\&    });
.Ve
.PP
Creates a new instance of Koha::Devel::CI::IncrementalRuns. The constructor accepts a hash reference with the following keys:
\&\- `incremental_run`: A flag indicating whether to run incrementally the tests [default env \s-1KOHA_CI_INCREMENTAL_RUNS\s0]
\&\- `git_repo_dir`: The directory where the Git repository is stored [default /tmp/koha\-ci\-results]
\&\- `repo_url`: The \s-1URL\s0 of the Git repository [default env \s-1KOHA_CI_INCREMENTAL_RUN_REPO_URL\s0]
\&\- `report`: A flag indicating whether to report the results [default env \s-1KOHA_CI_INCREMENTAL_RUNS_REPORT\s0]
\&\- `token`: The token for authenticating with the Git repository [default env \s-1KOHA_CI_INCREMENTAL_RUNS_TOKEN\s0]
\&\- `test_name`: The name of the test [default name of the test]
\&\- `context`: The context for file exclusions
.SS "get_files_to_test"
.IX Subsection "get_files_to_test"
.Vb 1
\&    my @files_to_test = $ci\->get_files_to_test(\*(Aqpl\*(Aq);
.Ve
.PP
Determines the list of files to be tested based on the incremental run settings. If incremental runs are enabled, it retrieves the list of files that have been modified since the last build. Otherwise, it retrieves all relevant files.
.SS "report_results"
.IX Subsection "report_results"
.Vb 1
\&    $ci\->report_results($results);
.Ve
.PP
Reports the results of the tests by committing the list of failures to the Git repository. This method is called only if the `report` flag is set.
